summary:
  A drawing is never asked for its shape and is read like any picture.

history:
  When the cover began to be read with no fitting mode, so that a small
  logo could say its own size, a drawing was caught in it. An SVG named so
  came back 600 by 600 whatever its shape and a logo of 200 by 80 was drawn
  squeezed into the square; one kept without its extension came back at the
  200 by 80 it declares and was drawn blurred. A drawing is asked for its
  shape and rendered into a box of that shape. This mutant gives it no box.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverImage.qml

find:
      readonly property var _box: CoverLogic.box(_shape.width, _shape.height, 600)

replace:
      readonly property var _box: CoverLogic.box(0, 0, 600)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cover_larger_fetch.py::test_a_drawing_from_the_network_is_asked_for_its_shape_once,
  which runs first, with a drawing from the network, and behind it by
  tests/qml/tst_coverimage.qml::test_a_drawing_keeps_its_shape_and_is_rendered_for_the_frame,
  which reads drawings that are local files.
  Line-neutral.
